ard T."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"[Ottowa] : Carleton University, 1982"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)761407339"}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Philip E. Uren Memorial lecture ; 1982"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990099011920203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0770901336"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"10278931"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"DK4442 .D38 1982"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990099011920203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"009901192"}},"processingDate":"2023-04-27T08:06Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"VA@"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"840109"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20060423"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990099011920203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"titleInfo":[{"title":"Auschwitz and the Second World War in Poland =","subTitle":"Auschwitz i druga wojna światowa w Polsce"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Auschwitz i druga wojna światowa w Polsce"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Auschwitz i druga wojna światowa w Polsce"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Auschwitz i druga wojna światowa w Polsce"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Representations of Auschwitz"}],"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Davies, Norman.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Flis, Andrzej"}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Conference papers and proceedings"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"pl"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Poland"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Kraków"}}],"publisher":"Universitas","dateIssued":["c1997",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1997"}],"edition":"Wyd. 1.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":[{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"pol"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"Polish"}]},{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}}],"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"74 p. : port. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Analyzes misunderstandings related to the memory of wartime events in Poland due to lack of proper information about their complexity. Few people outside of Poland are aware that Auschwitz was composed of three camps, and that in Auschwitz I thousands of Polish prisoners died. Remarks that it is unfortunate that Auschwitz has been adopted as the international symbol of the Holocaust. Treblinka would be more proper as its symbol. States that those who accuse the non-Jewish population of not helping the condemned Jews are not aware of the terror which affected all the inhabitants of occupied Poland. Discusses, as well, racial segregation, collaboration, and resistance in Poland. Few people know that, after the war, Nazis and Polish non-communist fighters (e.g. members of the Home Army) were imprisoned together by the new communist regime. Soviet misinformation about recent history also led to false understanding of the tragedies which occurred on Polish soil."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Norman Davies."},"\"A lecture given at the Representations of Auschwitz international conference at the Jagiellonian University, July 1995.\"",{"@type":"bi